==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (High-Yield)]] spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Fireworks Guys (Low-Yield)]] spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Firecracker]] (6,000%) spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*2 [[Firecracker]]s (6,000%) spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
*3 [[Firecracker]]s (6,000%) spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
*4 [[Firecracker]]s (6,000%) spawn after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
*5 [[Firecracker]]s (6,000%) spawn after 63.33 seconds<sup>1,900f</sup>, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Firecracker]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**45 [[Firecracker]]s (6,000%) spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
**30 [[Firecracker]]s (6,000%) spawn, delay 2~3 seconds<sup>60f~90f</sup>.
**15 [[Firecracker]]s (6,000%) spawn, delay 3~4 seconds<sup>90f~120f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The start of the stage will have some Firecrackers, so try using a wave unit like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] or [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan]], but Crazed Sexy Legs  is easier to use. When you hit the base, lots of Firecrackers will show up and continously knock-back your units. The key is to use attackers with large area damage so that the Firecrackers don't wreak that much havoc on your frontline. [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is great at this, having massive damage against Red and even being able to pierce the frontline with his [[Long Distance]]. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] can also be good at this role. If you somehow own [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] by this time, he can be an amazing asset to create the brightest fireworks show you've ever seen.

